{"connection_id": "BC-6064e4e3d4f8922768af", "ref": "WLC:Gen.31.48", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "adı konmuş tanık yığını", "note": "Lavan taş yığınının iki taraf arasında tanık olduğunu söyleyip ona Galed adını verir; yükseltilmiş nesne, ad ve ilişkinin tanınmasını aynı anda taşır."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b268c3261d5ce0d905c9", "ref": "WLC:Gen.32.29", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the divine wrestler's name withheld", "note": "The commentary defines a name as what lets one know its bearer; Jacob asks the divine wrestler's name but receives the reply “Why do you ask my name?”, setting a limit on that knowledge."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2c1a0ceb636a1191dcde", "ref": "WLC:Gen.32.30", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "a place named after seeing God", "note": "The commentary says a name is a sign by which a reality is recognized; Jacob names the place Peniel after seeing God face to face, turning an encounter into a place-name."}
{"connection_id": "BC-56dd88b3e30b20efd022", "ref": "WLC:Gen.33.20", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Arabic Allah / Hebrew El", "note": "The commentary names Allah in 1:1; Arabic Allah and Hebrew El/Eloah are related Semitic divine terms, while Jacob names an altar El-Elohe-Israel. The terms are cognate, not identical titles."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f322a1a7293314a72856", "ref": "WLC:Gen.4.15", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Cain's sign protects its bearer", "note": "The commentary's camel brand lets observers recognize its bearer; Genesis says God gives Cain a sign so that anyone finding him will not kill him, though it does not say the sign is a bodily brand."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b1a2e9f27b7aa038bc87", "ref": "WLC:Gen.4.15", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "Kayin'in korunma işareti", "note": "Tanrı Kayin'i bulanların onu öldürmemesi için üzerine işaret koyar; Kur'an'daki buruna vurulacak cezalandırıcı damgaya karşı, tanınabilir işaret burada koruyucudur."}
{"connection_id": "BC-21f67632739306ab9b94", "ref": "WLC:Gen.4.26", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "calling on the divine name", "note": "The commentary includes calling Allah by name; Genesis says people began to call on the name of YHWH, an early narrative use of invocation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5844957aaf5e0623e59c", "ref": "WLC:Gen.4.26", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "adı çağırmak", "note": "Enoş günlerinde YHWH adını çağırmaya başlanır; yorumdaki Ya Allah diye seslenme ve adla başlangıç için eski bir çağrı örneğidir."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bda4447a4076cb720cd1", "ref": "WLC:Gen.40.8", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Joseph speaks to fellow prisoners", "note": "The commentary's Qur'an 12:40 places Joseph's religious speech among prison companions; in Genesis 40:8 he tells two inmates that interpretations belong to God. Genesis does not discuss their idols, so the shared prison speech makes the difference in subject clear."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e8318e48de1e65f3dd67", "ref": "WLC:Gen.7.1", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Noah and the ark's boarding", "note": "The commentary cites Noah addressing those boarding the ark; Genesis has YHWH command Noah and his household to enter it, preserving the shared boarding scene but assigning the speech to God."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f009e2f864f7d3b8d26f", "ref": "WLC:Gen.7.1", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Nuh'a gemiye girme buyruğu", "note": "YHWH Nuh'a bütün eviyle gemiye girmesini buyurur; yorumdaki Nuh'un gemiye binme çağrısının aynı tufan eşiğini, fakat ilâhî ad formülü olmadan, verir."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b3ba98d5ef42f990bc55", "ref": "WLC:Gen.8.16", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Nuh'a gemiden çıkma buyruğu", "note": "Sular çekilince Tanrı Nuh'a gemiden çıkmasını söyler; Kur'an'daki geminin yürüyüşü ve duruşunun adla anılması yanında varış ve duruş anını tamamlar."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0e981919fe840fe98106", "ref": "WLC:Gen.8.4", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "the ark comes to rest", "note": "The commentary says Noah places the ark's sailing and mooring under God's name; Genesis reports that the ark came to rest on Ararat without naming that action as an invocation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-82c65126383f9e930780", "ref": "WLC:Gen.9.13", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "rainbow as covenant sign", "note": "The commentary defines an identifying trace; God sets the bow in the cloud as a sign of the covenant between God and earth, adding a visible sign that recalls a relation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8686ff054e92d496db4a", "ref": "WLC:Gen.9.13", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "buluttaki antlaşma yayı", "note": "Tanrı yayını buluta koyup onu kendisi ile yeryüzü arasındaki antlaşmanın işareti kılar; bütün göğe asılmış tanınabilir iz, yorumdaki yükseltilmiş alamet imgesini kozmik ölçekte işler."}
