{"connection_id": "BC-f7aabf72fe9cfed8e027", "ref": "WLC:Num.15.39", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "a visible fringe prompts recognition", "note": "The commentary says reading a mark means seeing a trace; Israelites are to see the fringes, remember the commandments, and do them, making a worn sign a prompt to recognize and obey."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3e00618096d7efeb8442", "ref": "WLC:Num.15.39", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "görüp hatırlatan püskül", "note": "Püskül görülür, YHWH'nin buyrukları hatırlanır ve uygulanır; iz okununca bilgi ve davranış doğması, tevesseme ile anlatılan işleyişe yakındır."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c89c206ac6f4ebaf144a", "ref": "WLC:Num.17.3", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "names written on tribal staffs", "note": "The commentary links names with identifying marks; the tribal leaders' names are written on their staffs, and Aaron's name is written on Levi's staff."}
